Description: This package implement distributions for 
  correlation/covariance matrices including two approachs 
  to model correlation matrices from a graphical structure.
  One use the latent parent variable framework as
  proposed in <https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.06289>.
  The other uses a graph to specify conditional 
  relations between the variables.
  The graphical structure makes correlation matrices 
  interpretable and avoids the quadratic increase of 
  parameters as a function of the dimension. 
  These two modeling classes are then used as prior for
  latent model parameters. 
  In the first approach a natural sequence of simpler 
  models along with a complexity penalization is used.
  The second penalizes deviations from a base model.
  Models are implemented in a C code template for 
  the 'cgeneric' interface with the 'INLA' package 
  (<https://www.r-inla.org>). 
  This allows one to use 'INLA' to build and fit 
  complex data models using the models in this 
  package as building blocks.
